Dial is from numbers 0 to 99 in order
Input = A sequence of rotations
    L is towards lower numbers
    R is towards higher numbers
    # is the distance you have to rotate
Rotational - possible to go left from 0 to 99 or right 99 to 0
    Modulo needed at a 100?
    -1 % 100 = 99 <- so negative numbers will work in modulo
How many times is the number left pointing at 0?


Part 2:
    Same rotation method, but now checking how many times it crosses over 0 instead of it being exactly 0

Ex: 
    Step_1: 50
    L68
    Step_2: 82 <- Update Password (Went over 0)
        Modulo 100 = 82 but still 0, 82
    L23
    Step 3: 50 <- No update required

Idea: 
    Basically check if
        1. Curr_Location - Rotation < 0 if going left
        2. Curr_Location + Rotation > 100 if going right
    OR  
        1. Rotation > 100 - Curr_Location if R
        2. Rotation > Curr_Location - 0 if L 
    Then we passed over 0 
        I.e if modulo triggered??
    



build command:
    clang Day1Puzzle1.c -o Day1Puzzle1
run by calling:
    ./Day1Puzzle1

